{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Midsummer’s Pilgrimage to Japan’s Fair and Noble Lands**\n\n**Act I: Scene I – The Land of the Rising Sun**\n\n*Enter THOU fair traveler into the bustling streets of Tokyo.*\n\n**Day One: The Imperial Metropolis**\nUpon thy arrival in Edo’s modern guise where neon doth dance with ancient stones thou shalt begin thy quest.\n- **Morning:** Pray at the sacred Meiji Shrine where the kami do dwell in quiet grace.\n- **Noon:** Feast upon sushi as fresh as spring’s first bloom at Tsukiji’s Outer Market.\n- **Afternoon:** Wander through Asakusa’s Senso-ji where incense curls like spirits’ breath and fortune’s slips flutter in the breeze.\n- **Evening:** Behold the golden glow of Tokyo Tower piercing the twilight sky and dine upon yakitori in a lantern-lit izakaya.\n\n**Day Two: The Floating World and the Sacred Peaks**\n- **Dawn:** Board the swift Shinkansen bound for Kyoto the thousand-year-old.\n- **Midday:** Enter the gates of Fushimi Inari where fox spirits keep watch o’er crimson torii paths that climb the mountain’s spine.\n- **Dusk:** Admire the koi fish in Arashiyama’s bamboo groves and sup upon tofu as pure as the moon.\n\n**Act II: Scene II – The Ancient Capital**\n\n*Enter thee into Kyoto’s embrace where time itself doth kneel.*\n\n**Day Three: Temples and Tea**\n- **Morrow:** Seek the Kinkaku-ji where the golden pavilion gleams upon the mirror pond.\n- **Noon:** Partake in the sacred art of tea at Camellia’s gentle hands.\n- **Afternoon:** Lose thyself in Gion’s lanes where geisha may flit like will-o’-the-wisps.\n- **Evening:** Dine upon kaiseki as artful as a poet’s verse.\n\n**Day Four: The Path of the Samurai**\n- **Dawn:** Journey to Nara’s hallowed grounds where deer bow like courtiers.\n- **Midday:** Worship at Todai-ji where the Great Buddha sits in silent majesty.\n- **Dusk:** Return to Kyoto and wander through Pontocho’s narrow ways lit by paper lanterns.\n\n**Act III: Scene III – The Island of Spirits**\n\n*Enter now into the mystic isle of Miyajima.*\n\n**Day Five: The Tide’s Embrace**\n- **Morning:** Cross the Seto Inland Sea to Miyajima where the torii stands where tide and earth do meet.\n- **Noon:** Climb Mount Misen and spy the Inland Sea spread below like a painter’s dream.\n- **Evening:** Watch the sun dip low and paint the torii gates in hues of fire.\n\n**Act IV: Scene IV – The Northern Realm**\n\n*Upon thy return to the capital of the shogun.*\n\n**Day Six: Edo’s Lasting Splendor**\n- **Dawn:** Seek the Edo-Tokyo Museum where past and present do waltz.\n- **Noon:** Stroll through Ueno’s parks where cherry blossoms may yet linger.\n- **Dusk:** Farewell Tokyo with a final toast upon a rooftop where the city’s heart beats loud and bright.\n\n**Epilogue: The Traveler’s Farewell**\nThus dost thy journey end in this fair land where each stone and stream doth whisper tales of old. May thy heart be light and thy steps swift as thou returnest to thine own realm bearing memories as precious as gold.\n\n*Exeunt omnes, with the sun’s descent.*", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.5875226259231567}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.05178029462695122}, {"token": " M", "logprob": -0.8411155343055725}, {"token": "ids", "logprob": -0.014771614223718643}, {"token": "ummer", "logprob": -6.317892984952778e-05}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.06951607763767242}, {"token": " Pil", "logprob": -1.117056131362915}, {"token": "gr", "logprob": -9.417489309271332e-06}, {"token": "image", "logprob": -1.680836794548668e-05}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.07678379863500595}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -3.421464204788208}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.06704875826835632}, {"token": " Fair", "logprob": -0.07272516191005707}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.45860278606414795}, {"token": " Noble", "logprob": -1.6254992485046387}, {"token": " Lands", "logprob": -0.08149772882461548}, {"token": "**\n\n